---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { APK } from '../data/apk';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';
---
<Base title="Privacy & Permissions — MJ PDF 3.1.0" description="What MJ PDF 3.1.0 asks for on Android, what is verified about its privacy, and what is not claimed." path="/privacy/" crumbs={[{name:'Privacy',path:'/privacy/'}]}>
  <div class="wrap page-h"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Privacy</nav>
    <h1>Privacy &amp; <span class="grad">permissions</span></h1>
    <p class="lead" style="margin-top:1rem">What can be verified about MJ PDF 3.1.0, stated plainly and without exaggeration.</p></div>
  <section class="sec" style="padding-top:20px"><div class="wrap narrow prose">
    <h2>What is verified</h2>
    <ul class="checks"><li>MJ PDF is open source under the GPL-3.0 license, so its code can be inspected on <a href={SITE.links.source} rel="noopener">GitLab</a>.</li><li>The app contains no advertising.</li><li>Your PDFs are opened and rendered on your device.</li><li>Incognito mode is available in the reader menu.</li></ul>
    <div class="note"><strong>About trackers.</strong> The project documentation states that Exodus Privacy reports a tracker in MJ PDF, and the APK bundles the ACRA crash-reporting library. This website therefore does not claim "zero tracking" or "no data collection". Review the source code and the Exodus report for details.</div>
    <h2>Permissions in the 3.1.0 APK</h2>
    <div class="card"><table class="spec"><tbody>{APK.permissions.map(([p, d]) => <tr><th scope="row" class="mono">{p}</th><td>{d}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>This site is static. It has no accounts, forms, advertising scripts or analytics code. Downloading the APK from this site is a plain file download.</p>
    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>Open an issue on the <a href={SITE.links.mirror} rel="noopener">GitHub mirror</a> or the GitLab project, or read the <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a>.</p>
  </div></section>
</Base>
